{{h1}}Development Best Practices

{{h2}}Reuse Code and Patterns

- Check for existing code, established patterns, and shared utilities before introducing new functionality.
- Reuse and improve established infrastructure instead of reimplementing it.
- Reduce needless duplication by extracting or combining repeated code and patterns when that improves clarity and maintenance.
- Keep justified duplication where combining it would obscure distinct domain behaviour or create an inappropriate dependency.
